# dependencies
node_modules/

# secrets — .env holds AI provider keys; only .env.example is tracked
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
secrets.env

# logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# editor / tool state
# Impeccable keeps three different things in here and they do not belong on the same side of this
# line. config.json is the SHARED design-detector config — which rules are ignored for this project
# and why — so it is a project decision and belongs in the repo. config.local.json is explicitly
# per-developer, and hook.cache.json is per-session scratch. Ignoring the whole directory meant a
# "shared" ignore was never shared: it would not survive a fresh clone or a second machine.
# `**/` because there is more than one of these: the detector writes beside whichever directory the
# CLI was run from, so there is one at the repo root and one under app/. A root-anchored pattern
# covered only the first, and the second was being held back by .git/info/exclude — which is local
# to one clone and would not protect anybody else.
**/.impeccable/*
!**/.impeccable/config.json

# per-student saves, when the file backend is in use (`npm start` on a laptop). Hosted, these live
# in a KV store instead — see app/store.js. This is somebody's actual work, not build output, so it
# is ignored rather than cleaned.
app/.data/

# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# scratch
*.bak
